  "root_cause": {
    "text": "In the powerpc/xive subsystem, the `xive_irq_free_data()` function incorrectly retrieved the `struct xive_irq_data` using `irq_get_chip_data()`, which queried the child interrupt domain instead of the parent XIVE domain where the data was stored, preventing memory deallocation.",
    "evidence": "The CVE description states that after commit cc0cc23babc9, `xive_irq_free_data()` used `irq_get_chip_data()` looking up data through the child domain, while the XIVE-specific data is associated with the XIVE (parent) domain; the patch fixes this by passing the `domain` pointer to `xive_irq_free_data()` and using `irq_domain_get_irq_data(domain, virq)` to access the correct parent domain data.",
    "passed_review": true
  },
